<section class="section architecture-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Architecture in public</p>
      <h2 id="architecture-title">Keep authority close to the work.</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core">RepoPact Core source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </div>
  <div class="architecture-layout">
    <div class="architecture-copy">
      <p>RepoPact Core treats the repository as the authoritative record for project intent, scope, work state, decisions, and evidence. Its CLI and Workbench are clients of a canonical semantic engine; dashboards and graph views remain derived views.</p>
      <p>This diagram documents RepoPact Core. The other ForgeWire Labs projects have their own architecture and release boundaries.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ site.basePath }}/engineering/">See the design boundaries <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
    <figure class="architecture-figure">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg" alt="RepoPact Core architecture diagram from its public repository. Authoritative repository records feed the canonical Rust engine and CLI or Workbench clients; dashboards and graph views are derived, optional integrations have separate boundaries, and evidence records observed results." width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>RepoPact Core architecture and authority boundaries · Source: its public architecture documentation.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

